<title>ITALY: Italy's Turin sees prelim Jan CPI at 0.0 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Italy's Turin sees prelim Jan CPI at 0.0 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Turin said its January consumer price index stood at 0.0 percent month-on-month and 2.6 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In December, Turin's inflation rate was 0.0 percent and 2.5 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Turin is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 8.81 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to December 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.0   (0.0)     2.6  (2.5)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.3   (0.1)     2.2  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	  -0.1   (0.2)     5.8  (6.4)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.7   (0.0)     4.2  (3.5)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0   (0.0)     2.1  (1.0)</p>
<p>    Health services		   1.8   (0.0)     1.7  (0.8)</p>
<p>    Transportation		   -0.3   (0.0)     2.8  (2.5)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -1.4   (0.0)     0.9  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0   (0.0)     2.0 (-2.4)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0   (0.0)     1.7  (1.1)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.1   (0.0)     2.4  (2.0)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
